---
description: Core project architecture and source-of-truth rules for the workout app
alwaysApply: true
---

- Build a single-user local-first iOS workout logger in SwiftUI.
- Use SQLite via GRDB for persistence unless the project explicitly switches away later.
- Use a layered structure:
  - Domain: pure models and rules
  - Persistence: database, migrations, repositories
  - Services: timer, history matching, PRs, import, coaching
  - ViewModels: screen state and user actions
  - UI: SwiftUI views only
- The source of truth is normalized tables, not nested JSON blobs.
- The primary entities are:
  - Exercise
  - ExerciseAlias
  - WorkoutSession
  - WorkoutSessionExercise
  - WorkoutBlock
  - SetEntry
  - ActiveWorkoutState
  - RestTimerState
  - WorkoutTemplate
  - WorkoutTemplateExercise
- Keep business rules out of SwiftUI view files.
- Make all user actions work offline.
- Treat remote sync as optional mirroring, not required for core behavior.
